## 2. rlxfw's own kernel files — `GPL-2.0-only`, and the choice is forced

**Covered:** every file under `config/rlxfw-src/`: the compiled sources, the
ones declared and not built (`rtl819x-spi-write.c`, behind
`CONFIG_MTD_RTL819X_WRITE`, which the mainline configuration does not set) and
the headers. The directory is the unit, and no count of it is kept here: one
went stale the day a header was added.

The 12 compiled sources are `rlxfw-devices`, `rlxfw_mark`, `rlxfw-entropy`,
`rtl819x-timer`, `rtl819x-gpio`, `rtl819x-keys`, `rtl819x-spi`, `rtl819x-wdt`,
`rtl819x-nic`, `rtl819x-switch`, `rtl819x-view` and `rlxfw-seam`
(`docs/sbom.md` row `K6`).

**Why GPL-2.0-*only* and not "or later".**

1. 量 at `01cff02b`, all 16 files then present are paths the vendor drop does
   not have: they are additions to the staged tree, not edits of vendor files.
   So nothing about them is inherited file-by-file; the question is what the
   link decides.
2. 讀 the drop's `linux-2.6.30/COPYING` is the GPL version 2 text with the
   kernel's own preamble note, and the kernel is distributed under version 2
   with no "or later" option. A file linked into that kernel and distributed as
   part of it cannot be offered to the recipient under version 3.
3. 量 the build links them into one monolithic `vmlinux`: in the configuration
   the board ran, `CONFIG_MODULES` is not set and no `.ko` exists
   (`docs/sbom.md` § 1), so there is not even a loadable-module argument to
   have.
4. 讀 one of the 12 already says so in the only machine-readable way the kernel
   has: `rtl819x-wdt.c` carries `MODULE_LICENSE("GPL")`, which the kernel reads
   as a declaration of GPL compatibility. 量 it is the only such declaration in
   rlxfw's own code; the other 11 carry no licence text of any kind.

So `GPL-2.0-only` records what the link already decided.

**🔴 The per-file statement cannot go at the top of the file, and that is a
measurement rather than a style choice.** 量 2026-10-04 over `git ls-files
'*.md'`: these twelve basenames are cited **by line number 213 times, 115 of
them distinct**, and **108 of the citing lines are in 15 files `citecheck`
reads** — `SPEC.md` 28, `notes/nic-driver.md` 21, `docs/nic-vendor-diff.md` 17,
`docs/KNOWN-ISSUES.md` 10, and eleven more. An `SPDX-License-Identifier` line
inserted as line 1 shifts every line in the file by one and rots all 108 at
once, and `spec-check`'s `C11` token-checks this exact population by basename,
so both checkers would go red. The rest of the 213 are in `LOG.md` and in frozen
`bench/` cards, which resolve historically and must not be renumbered at all
(讀 `CLAUDE.md`).

So the per-file statement is made where it moves no line: a licence comment at
the **end** of each file, or one `config/rlxfw-src/LICENSE` naming the directory.
`SPDX-License-Identifier` wants line 1 by convention, and that convention
postdates this 2.6.30 tree by eight years and is not enforced anywhere in this
build — so the convention is what gives way, and this paragraph is why.

**What this costs and where.** 🔴 讀 `tools/rlxfw-kbuild.sh` computes
`RECIPE_ID` as a sha256 over **every file under `config/`**, comments included,
and compiles it into the kernel as `-DRLXFW_SRC_ID`. Adding an SPDX line to a
file under `config/rlxfw-src/` therefore moves `RECIPE_ID` and invalidates the
identity assertion of any card that quotes the old value. 量 2026-10-04 it has
**already moved** this gate — `bb0f1a5f`, against the `0e45c61d` that
`docs/sbom.md` records for cell `f184a` — because `config/fix-cases.toml` and
`config/r9-probes.toml` landed in `76d0a121`. So the headers cost a rebuild
that is already owed, and nothing new. (量 computed with the formula at
`tools/rlxfw-kbuild.sh`'s `RECIPE_ID` assignment, run under Git Bash on DrvFs;
the two shells' `find` orderings were not cross-checked, so the claim that
carries weight is *it is not `0e45c61d`*, not the exact eight hex digits.)

