## 8. What this file does not establish

- **It is not a legal opinion**, and saying so once is the point of the first
  paragraph rather than a disclaimer repeated per section.
- **It does not establish who holds the copyright** in rlxfw's own code. "Own"
  throughout is a statement about provenance — no imported source, no
  `IMPORTED` marker, first commit in this repository — which is
  `docs/sbom.md`'s definition, not a chain of title.
- **It does not make the image distributable, and it discharges nothing.** 量
  0 of the 17 `file` rows in `config/rlxfw-initramfs.tsv` is a notice, so the
  image carries none. `v0.2`–`v0.6` carry no binary (量 2026-10-08, no assets);
  the binaries `v1.0` is made with travel only with their corresponding-source
  archive and the licence texts — this file among them — beside them, as assets
  of the same release (`offer.md` § 0). `offer.md` also names the two gaps
  (`SBOM-3`, `SBOM-4`) still open; `docs/release-process.md` is the order in
  which the release is made.
- **It does not close `SBOM-2`.** 35 Realtek-directory sources plus 3 in the
  loader stub carry no licence text; their licence is read from a `COPYING` file
  and that reading is not this project's to make authoritative.
- **It does not cover the loader on the unit** (`SBOM-7`): the Realtek bootcode
  2014.04.22 v1.3 is neither built nor shipped here.
- **It settles no number.** Every count above is quoted from `docs/sbom.md` or
  re-derived from the tree at the commit that adds this file; where a count has
  moved, `docs/sbom.md` is the owner and this file is the stale copy.
